1. CHANNEL LIST ON ITS OWN PAGE (Adam: 'no reason we should have to go to
   riders'): New channel list button on /operations/[tour]/channel-list —
   creates the standalone document, seeds its channel_list section (16 blank
   rows), attaches tour-wide, and says so: 'Assigned to every show on this
   tour — it will appear in the tour's rider automatically.'
2. RIDER-CENTRIC CATALOG (migration 263): the advance-centric presets
   ('Wi-Fi available', 'On-site washer' — venue answers) become artist
   demands: 13 templates rewritten/new — Hospitality Rider, Dressing Rooms,
   Catering/Buyout, Backline, Audio/PA, Lighting, Security & Barricade,
   Merch, Parking & Access, Towels & Laundry, Bus Stock, Guest List &
   Passes, Production Office. Idempotent re-seed; user rows untouched.
3. NATIVE CONTROL KILL (globals.css): per-theme color-scheme (class-scoped,
   light mode safe), orange accent-color on every native checkbox/radio,
   and .lp-select (token colors + custom chevron, appearance:none) applied
   to the raw selects in the rider builder + income slide-over.
4. THE FULL SETTLEMENT WATERFALL (wires migration 262 — paste 262 now):
   computeBoxOffice engine (gross BO → facility/ticket/CC fees → net BO →
   expenses → split pool → artist share @ deal % → bonus tier → suggested
   overage; greater-of expressed as overage over the guarantee), the Deal &
   box office card, explicit 'Apply to Overage' (the click is the consent —
   never auto-written), BO-fee deduction kinds split out of the guarantee
   walk (Σ to the income cascade UNCHANGED), and the CATCH-UP BATCH panel:
   check past-unsettled shows, Settle N at contracted guarantee (Full &
   Final toggle, default on) through the EXISTING route sequentially so the
   income cascade runs per show with zero new money paths.

