Adam: rooms added on the hotel grid flooded the budget with 'unassigned
hotel' lines, and new rooms showed on Matrix + Cards but not Nights.

- ROOT CAUSE 1 (the flood): the rooming grid's save path auto-created a NEW
  hotel named 'Unassigned Hotel' per uncovered date with a zero-night
  same-day range. Placeholders are now named 'Hotel — {city} · {date}'
  (city from routing), span a true one night (checkout = next-day 00:00),
  are REUSED per date instead of duplicated, and legacy 'Unassigned Hotel'
  rows self-heal in place as you keep editing. No migration.
- BUDGET LABEL (Adam's exact ask): derived Accommodation lines now read
  '{hotel} — {city} · {check-in date} · {N rooms}', e.g.
  'Hotel Krasnapolsky — Amsterdam · 2026-08-12 · 3 rooms'. sourceId stays
  the hotel id, so existing lines relabel in place (draft versions; an
  APPROVED version's labels stay frozen by the lock policy, actuals move).
- ROOT CAUSE 2 (the middle tab): NOT the assumed zero-night filter — Matrix
  and Cards read live client data while Nights rendered the page-load RSC
  snapshot, and no rooming write ever called router.refresh(). Grid saves
  and deletes now refresh the snapshot; Nights updates like the others.
- Shared placeholder naming/detection helper (nightsSummary) also drives
  the rooming PDF + XLSX 'unassigned' special-casing.

