From eb923599edf9baf56cb268c05c6fdd15bb93cb0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Rowley <adamgrowley@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 04:29:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(nav+keys): the spine morph fires from the Day rail's
 Routing toggle; the TB keyboard grammar carries to every surface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Day → Routing now folds (Adam: 'why doesn't the slide over routing work
  on the day views?'): DayRail's Routing toggle was a plain <Link> that
  bypassed useSpineNavigate — the rail's day ENTRIES morphed, the toggle
  didn't. Same trigger, same modified-click guards.
- The tour-builder keyboard contract (Tab never walks a list · Enter
  commits + advances · arrows move the highlight · Enter is never dead)
  enforced everywhere it was missing:
  · BrandedSelect: Tab inside the open menu committed nothing and walked
    options — now commits the focused option and moves on (Shift+Tab back).
  · PositionPicker: Tab walked filter → every slot → Clear → Manage — now
    commits and advances; filter Tab commits the first free filtered slot.
  · Mic/DI combobox: Enter picked but never advanced; Enter with no
    highlight was dead — both fixed (onEnterCommit seam, keyboard-only).
  · ChannelListEditor: the missing advanceFrom('mic') wired.
  · EntityRefEditor (payroll/flights/commissions grids): arrows now move a
    real highlight, Enter picks it, Tab picks then commits-and-moves-right
    instead of committing a stale draft.
  · Settlement adders: Enter in amount/label/date fields submits (was dead).
Gates: tsc 0 · eslint 0 · vitest 538/538.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014d3AoWFQevqQHtrWLX5Tki
